<li><span id="source-2"></span><a href="https://asianethnology.org/article/1825/download">Rice Rituals of Orissa</a>, p. 242, on observances during the growth of paddy. <a href="#ref-2">↩</a></li>
<li><span id="source-3"></span><a href="https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/garba-of-gujarat-01962">Garba of Gujarat, UNESCO</a>, on the vessel, lamp and worship of Amba. <a href="#ref-3">↩</a></li>
<li><span id="source-4"></span><a href="/culture/osha/nuakhai/">Nuakhai, Project Odisha</a>, with <a href="https://journals.ub.uni-frankfurt.de/paideuma/index.php/paideuma/article/download/2046/2237/4542">Kesavan’s Bargarh fieldwork</a>. <a href="#ref-4">↩</a></li>
<li><span id="source-5"></span><a href="https://www.pib.gov.in/newsite/erelcontent.aspx?lang=2&amp;reg=48&amp;relid=14929">Press Information Bureau account of Pongal</a>. <a href="#ref-5">↩</a></li>
<li><span id="source-6"></span><a href="/culture/osha/manabasa-gurubara/">Manabasa Gurubara, Project Odisha</a>, with <a href="https://magazines.odisha.gov.in/orissareview/2018/Jun-July/engpdf/june-july-or-2018.pdf">Ghadai’s reading</a> of the Lakshmi Purana and description of the grain measure. <a href="#ref-6">↩</a></li>
</ol>
<section class="article-reading-path" aria-label="Read the festival articles" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><h2 data-astro-cid-q224smgb="true">Read the festival articles</h2><nav aria-label="Read the festival articles" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><ul data-astro-cid-q224smgb><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/stories/akhi-muthi-anukula/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Akhi Muthi Anukula <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-description" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Follow the first handful of paddy seed from home to the field.</span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/culture/osha/raja-parba/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Raja Parba <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-description" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Resting the earth as the monsoon approaches.</span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/stories/garbhana-sankranti/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Garbhana Sankranti <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-description" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Prayers for the rice still growing in the field, and a comparison with Gujarat’s Garba.</span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/culture/osha/nuakhai/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Nuakhai <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-description" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Offering and sharing the first new rice in western Odisha.</span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/culture/osha/manabasa-gurubara/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Manabasa Gurubara <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-description" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>The grain measure, Lakshmi and the question of who may eat.</span></span></a></li></ul></nav></section><section id="series-stories" class="series-stories" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a><h2 data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>Stories in this series</h2><figure class="series-photograph" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a><a href="/stories/when-the-goddess-comes-to-the-wall/" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a><img src="/assets/osakothi/simanchala-nahaka-2019.jpg" srcset="/images/responsive/bf0bddd22f01f440-480.webp 480w, /images/responsive/0758c20944798c2a-960.webp 960w, /images/responsive/f724c81ba31fc220-1440.webp 1440w" sizes="(max-width: 470px) 90vw, 420px" decoding="async" alt="Guru Simanchala Nahaka performing Osakothi, holding a peacock-feather whisk above his head." width="2046" height="2838" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a="true"></a><figcaption data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>Guru Simanchala Nahaka performing Dhanakoila, also known as Osakothi, 5 August 2019. Photograph by <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guru_Simanchala_Nahaka_performs_Dhanakoila_or_Osakothi_(Gahana).jpg" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>Prateek Pattanaik</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Responsive versions resized and re-encoded without cropping.</figcaption></figure><h3 data-astro-cid-owyxto2a><a href="/stories/when-the-goddess-comes-to-the-wall/" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>When the Goddess Comes to the Wall <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>→</span></a></h3><p data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>In Ganjam’s Osakothi, painters, singers and families bring a sacred world into being, carrying hopes for the land and the lives it sustains.</p></section><p class="article-update" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a><a href="/contribute/?page=%2Fstories%2Fthe-year-that-feeds-us%2F" data-astro-cid-owyxto2a>Suggest an update</a>. GitHub submissions are public; omit private contact details and consent documents.</p></div></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div class="footer-intro"><a href="/" class="home-link" aria-label="Project Odisha home"><span class="brand brand-en" lang="en"><img class="brand-signature" src="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" alt="Project Odisha" width="850" height="140"></span></a><p>Discover Odisha. Imagine the possibilities.</p><p class="footer-mission">People, places and knowledge.<br>A story we build together.</p><div class="page-share" data-page-share data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf><button class="utk-button utk-button--secondary" type="button" data-share-button hidden data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf>Share this page</button><p data-share-status role="status" data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf></p><label data-share-fallback hidden data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf>Page link<input readonly type="url" aria-label="Page link to copy" data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf></label></div><script type="module" src="/_astro/PageShare.astro_astro_type_script_index_0_lang.ChO52ZaM.js"></script></div><nav class="footer-links" aria-label="About Project Odisha"><h2 class="eyebrow">The project</h2><a href="/about/">About the project</a><a href="/founder/">The founder</a><a href="/about/editorial-process/">Our editorial process</a><a href="/global-connections/">Global Connections</a></nav><nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Explore and contribute"><h2 class="eyebrow">Take part</h2><a href="/books/">Books</a><a href="/characters/">Character worlds</a><a href="/contribute/">Contribute</a><a href="/contribute/?page=%2Fstories%2Fthe-year-that-feeds-us%2F">Suggest a correction</a></nav><nav class="fo